master theoram for dividing funtion 
𝑇(𝑛) = 𝑎𝑇(𝑛/𝑏)+ O(n^k 𝑙𝑜𝑔^p n) 
a) a < b^k : if p < 0, then T(n) = O(n^k)
             if p ≥ 0, then T(n) = O(n^k 𝑙𝑜𝑔^𝑝 n) 
			 
b) a = b^k : if p < -1, then T(n) = O(n^k) 	
             if p = -1, then T(n) = O(n^k log log n)
             if p > -1, then T(n) = O(n^k 𝑙𝑜𝑔𝑝+1 n)
              
					 
c) a > b^k : T(n) = O(𝑛^𝑙𝑜𝑔𝑏𝑎)
